codex
The invariant is now fixed: at each loop head it summarizes the best result/score over the remaining symbolic string sequence, plus the final values of the loop target and temporary variable. I’m encoding string-only inputs as a symbolic `StrSeq` mapped structurally into the semantics’ `ValSeq`; this is not a size bound and is surjective onto every finite modeled list of strings. The planned proof extensions are all total definitional summaries with disjoint constructor/Boolean cases—no execution-bypassing rules or opaque program-derived values.
